{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "KSV-0009",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Access to host network"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sharing the host’s network namespace permits processes in the pod to communicate with processes bound to the host’s loopback adapter."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0009",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0009\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: Access to host network\nMessage: DaemonSet 'vanian-runtime-probe' should not set 'spec.template.spec.hostNetwork' to true\nLink: [KSV-0009](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0009)\nSharing the host’s network namespace permits processes in the pod to communicate with processes bound to the host’s loopback adapter.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0009**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|HIGH|Access to host network|DaemonSet 'vanian-runtime-probe' should not set 'spec.template.spec.hostNetwork' to true|[KSV-0009](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0009)|\n\nSharing the host’s network namespace permits processes in the pod to communicate with processes bound to the host’s loopback adapter."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0010",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Access to host PID"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Sharing the host’s PID namespace allows visibility on host processes, potentially leaking information such as environment variables and configuration."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0010",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0010\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: Access to host PID\nMessage: DaemonSet 'vanian-runtime-probe' should not set 'spec.template.spec.hostPID' to true\nLink: [KSV-0010](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0010)\nSharing the host’s PID namespace allows visibility on host processes, potentially leaking information such as environment variables and configuration.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0010**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|HIGH|Access to host PID|DaemonSet 'vanian-runtime-probe' should not set 'spec.template.spec.hostPID' to true|[KSV-0010](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0010)|\n\nSharing the host’s PID namespace allows visibility on host processes, potentially leaking information such as environment variables and configuration."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0118",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Default security context configured"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Security context controls the allocation of security parameters for the pod/container/volume, ensuring the appropriate level of protection. Relying on default security context may expose vulnerabilities to potential attacks that rely on privileged access."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0118",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0118\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: Default security context configured\nMessage: daemonset vanian-runtime-probe in default namespace is using the default security context, which allows root privileges\nLink: [KSV-0118](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0118)\nSecurity context controls the allocation of security parameters for the pod/container/volume, ensuring the appropriate level of protection. Relying on default security context may expose vulnerabilities to potential attacks that rely on privileged access.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0118**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|HIGH|Default security context configured|daemonset vanian-runtime-probe in default namespace is using the default security context, which allows root privileges|[KSV-0118](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0118)|\n\nSecurity context controls the allocation of security parameters for the pod/container/volume, ensuring the appropriate level of protection. Relying on default security context may expose vulnerabilities to potential attacks that rely on privileged access."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0121",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Kubernetes resource with disallowed volumes mounted"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HostPath present many security risks and as a security practice it is better to avoid critical host paths mounts."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0121",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0121\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: Kubernetes resource with disallowed volumes mounted\nMessage: daemonset vanian-runtime-probe in default namespace shouldn't have volumes set to {\"/proc\"}\nLink: [KSV-0121](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0121)\nHostPath present many security risks and as a security practice it is better to avoid critical host paths mounts.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0121**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|HIGH|Kubernetes resource with disallowed volumes mounted|daemonset vanian-runtime-probe in default namespace shouldn't have volumes set to {\"/proc\"}|[KSV-0121](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0121)|\n\nHostPath present many security risks and as a security practice it is better to avoid critical host paths mounts."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.76.2"
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "KSV-0009",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Artifact: validation/enterprise/results/HELM_20261028T103133Z/template-enabled.yaml\nType: kubernetes\nVulnerability KSV-0009\nSeverity: HIGH\nMessage: DaemonSet 'vanian-runtime-probe' should not set 'spec.template.spec.hostNetwork' to true\nLink: [KSV-0009](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0009)"
          },
          "locations": [
